statement:
Write \(c_{\mathrm{box}}\) for the particular absolute constant denoted by \(c\) in the proof of accepted fact ac9b8b86eb2548d3. That proof supplies \(0<c_{\mathrm{box}}<1\). Set \(c_{\mathrm{lex}}=c_{\mathrm{box}}/2\).

For every integer \(n\ge1\), integers \(m_1,\ldots,m_n\ge1\), endpoint \(b\in\prod_{i=1}^n\{0,\ldots,m_i\}\), and tilt \(\beta\in\mathbb R^n\), let

\[
\begin{aligned}
D&=\left\{I\in\prod_{i=1}^n\{0,\ldots,m_i\}:I\le_{\mathrm{lex}}b\right\},
&w_I&=\exp(-\beta\cdot I),
&W&=\sum_{I\in D}w_I,\\
\tau_w(J)&=\inf_{H\ni J}\sum_{I\in D\cap H}w_I,
&A&=\sum_{J\in D}w_J\tau_w(J).
\end{aligned}
\]

Here coordinate \(1\) is most significant in the lexicographic order, and the infimum is over closed halfspaces of the ambient space \(\mathbb R^n\). Then

\[
\begin{aligned}
\Sigma(b)
&=1+\sum_{\substack{1\le i\le n\\ b_i=1}}2^{n-i}
  +\sum_{\substack{1\le i\le n\\ b_i\ge2}}2^{n-i+1},\\
A&\ge \frac{c_{\mathrm{box}}W^2}{\Sigma(b)}
 \ge \frac{c_{\mathrm{box}}W^2}{2^{n+1}-1}
 \ge \frac{c_{\mathrm{lex}}}{2^n}W^2.
\end{aligned}
\]

These conclusions include singleton \(D\) and all prefixes of lower affine dimension.

In particular, suppose \(a_1,\ldots,a_n\) are nonnegative real numbers satisfying \(a_i>\sum_{j>i}a_jm_j\) for every \(1\le i\le n\), where an empty sum is zero. For every real \(b_{\mathrm{budget}}\ge0\), the complete lattice support

\[
D_{\mathrm{budget}}
=\left\{I\in\mathbb Z^n:0\le I_i\le m_i\ (1\le i\le n),\quad
          \sum_{i=1}^n a_iI_i\le b_{\mathrm{budget}}\right\}
\]

is a lexicographic prefix \(D\) as above. Thus the same average-depth estimate, with the same \(c_{\mathrm{lex}}\) and arbitrary \(\beta\), holds when \(D\) is replaced by \(D_{\mathrm{budget}}\). This support is the full box if and only if \(b_{\mathrm{budget}}\ge\sum_i a_im_i\).
